# iMBONi — Rules for Cline (simple)

Before you start:
1. Ask me: who am I (Marlene, Arcade, Gad, Cyusa or Doratha) and what is the task? Do not guess is not specified.
2. Read docs/PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md and my role file: docs/roles/<name>.md
3. Run `git status`. Never touch changes that are not mine.

While working:
4. Edit ONLY the folders that belong to my role.
5. If the task needs another person's folder: STOP. Tell me who to ask. Do not edit it.
6. Shared files (package.json, lockfiles, .env files, config, database migrations, route files): ask the owner first.
7. Do not invent API endpoints, response fields, database changes or school rules. If it is not agreed, ask.
8. Use what already exists. Do not create a second version of a feature.
9. Backend layers (Gad): routes -> controllers -> services -> repositories -> database. Rules in services, queries in repositories, never skip a layer.
10. Security: the server decides who can see what. A parent can only see their own children. Never put secrets in code.

When finished:
11. Tell me: files changed, tests run and their real results (say "NOT RUN" if not run), and what the next person must do.
12. Work on a branch (feature/<area>-<name>), small commits, never push straight to main.
13. read `PRS.md` and work accordingly
